# Line endings: LF in the repository and in every checkout, on every OS.
# Without this, git on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) checks files out with CRLF. The husky hooks
# then fail, because sh reads the \r at the end of each line as part of the command
# (`npx lint-staged\r`), and `npm run format:check` reports every file, because Prettier
# expects LF. `text=auto` leaves binary files alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
